<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <%# Per-page titles: set with `content_for :title` in a view.
        WCAG 2.4.2 - each page needs a title describing its topic. %>
    <title><%= content_for?(:title) ? "#{yield(:title)} | Stocks in the Future" : "Stocks in the Future" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, 'data-turbo-track': "reload" %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "actiontext", 'data-turbo-track': "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-slate-50" data-controller="drawer">
    <a href="#main-content" class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-2 focus:left-2 focus:z-100 focus:rounded-md focus:bg-sitf-primary focus:px-4 focus:py-2 focus:text-sitf-on-primary focus:outline-2 focus:outline-offset-2 focus:outline-sitf-primary-dark">Skip to main content</a>
    <% if user_signed_in? %>
      <%# Same treatment as the admin app bar: white against the slate-50 page, with the
          hairline bottom edge design.md blesses for fixed chrome. It was a full-width 1px bar
          in sitf-primary-dark (8.5:1, body-text weight for furniture), then briefly shadow-xs
          while the header was the same colour as the page. %>
      <%# px-4 lg:px-6 matches <main> below. As px-6 at every width the header's contents sat 24px in
          while the cards sat at 16px on a phone, so the chrome and the content did not share an edge. %>
      <header class="fixed top-0 left-0 w-full z-50 flex h-16 items-center justify-between border-b border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-4 lg:px-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <%# A button, not a label driving a hidden checkbox: a label is announced as a
              checkbox rather than as a control that opens navigation.

              No negative margin. The control's box is the thing that paints, so the box is what
              aligns to the gutter - flush with the cards below it at 16px. Two attempts at
              pulling it out to put the *glyph* on the gutter instead both failed, because
              whatever paints comes with it: first a filled button, then a hover fill, then a
              40px state layer, each hanging 6-8px past the content edge. The glyph sits 10px
              inside its own box because a 44px target centres a 24px icon; that is inherent, and
              it is the box the eye reads.

              rounded-lg, not rounded-full: design.md's radius token is `controls rounded-lg`.
              slate-600 on white is 7.58:1. %>
          <button type="button"
                  data-drawer-target="trigger"
                  data-action="drawer#toggle"
                  data-testid="open-navigation"
                  aria-expanded="false"
                  aria-controls="main-navigation"
                  class="lg:hidden flex min-h-11 min-w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-slate-600 transition-colors hover:bg-slate-100 hover:text-slate-900 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary">
            <span class="sr-only">Open navigation menu</span>
            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h16" />
            </svg>
          </button>
          <%= image_tag "SITF-Horz-no-tag-logo.svg", class: "h-8 w-auto", alt: "Stocks in The Future" %>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
          <div class="hidden lg:block">
            <%= render 'layouts/stock_ticker' %>
          </div>

          <%= render 'layouts/account_menu' %>
        </div>
      </header>

      <%= render 'layouts/navbar' %>

      <!-- Main: responsive margins and padding -->
      <main id="main-content" class="min-h-screen px-4 lg:px-6 ml-0 lg:ml-64 mt-16 pb-6 bg-slate-50">
        <%= render 'layouts/flash' %>

        <%= yield %>
      </main>
    <% else %>
      <%# Signed out there was no header at all, so the only route in was whatever page you
          happened to land on. The logo and one Sign in action, matching the signed-in bar. %>
      <header class="flex h-16 w-full items-center justify-between border-b border-slate-200 bg-white px-6 py-4">
        <%= link_to root_path, class: "inline-flex items-center rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary-dark" do %>
          <%= image_tag "SITF-Horz-no-tag-logo.svg", class: "h-8 w-auto", alt: "Stocks in The Future" %>
        <% end %>

        <% unless request.path == new_user_session_path %>
          <%= link_to "Sign in", new_user_session_path, class: "tw-btn-primary" %>
        <% end %>
      </header>

      <main id="main-content" class="min-h-screen p-4 lg:p-6 bg-slate-50">
        <%= render 'layouts/flash' %>

        <%= yield %>
      </main>
    <% end %>

    <!-- Trading Modal -->
    <%= render 'shared/modal' %>
  </body>
</html>
